Confirmed the real-world pattern (project.rs:1601-1615): the closure first clones the executor (or spawns a background task with `cx.background_executor().spawn(async move {...})`), then returns the future. My lecture's sample code `cx.on_app_quit(|cx| async move { cx.background_executor()... })` captures the `&mut App` borrow in the async block — that won't compile (the future must be `'static`, and `cx: &mut App` can't be moved into it; actually `async move` capturing `cx` by move would move the mutable reference, giving a lifetime error since Fut: 'static).

I need to fix the sample in 4.3.4 and in the 综合实践 to the correct pattern:

```rust
cx.on_app_quit(|cx| {
    let executor = cx.background_executor().clone();
    async move {
        eprintln!("[on_app_quit] 开始收尾……");
        executor.timer(Duration::from_millis(500)).await;
        eprintln!("[on_app_quit] 收尾完成");
    }
})
.detach();
```

